9 Jan;8(1):69-79.</strong></p> <p>Identification of Arg2443X in two unrelated A-T patients (Ae006: Arg2443X/Arg2443X, Ae015: Arg2443X/5546delT) The diagnosis of A-T was established based on typical clinical (ataxia, teleangiectasia) and laboratory findings (AFP, Ig) and confirmed in vitro by lab. evidence of X-ray or bleomycin sensitivity such as analysis of chromosome breakage rates or radio-resistant DNA synthesis or by flow cytometric analysis of cell-cycle abnormalities  after specific induction.</p> <p><strong>Telatar et al., <a title="American journal of human genetics." href="http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/9443866">Am J Hum Genet.</a> 1998 Jan;62(1):86-97.</strong></p> <p>1 African American A-T patient (genotype c.7327 C&gt;T p.Arg2443X/c.7926A&gt;T) whose cell line (AT3LA) was previously reported by Wright et al. (<a title="American journal of human genetics." href="http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/?term=Wright+ATM+1996">Am J Hum Genet.</a> <span class="highlight">1996</span> Oct;59(4):839-46.)</p> <p><strong> </strong></p> <p> </p>  [import GPD] Julia Bickmann 2015-04-22 17:36:41 -type: mutation details <p>Arg2443* is a known A-T mutation.</p> <p>c.7327C&gt;T p.Arg2443* + c.8264A&gt;C p.Tyr2755Ser (both het.) were observed in GS140213 (early-onset ataxia, no family history of ataxia, no other information given).</p>  "			ATM (inh=AR+AD oe_syn=0.97 oe_mis=0.93 oe_lof=0.80 pli=0.00), C11ORF65 (inh=AR+AD oe_syn=0.92 oe_mis=1.01 oe_lof=1.08 pli=0.00)
